Description

Winter 2027 Internship/Hybrid

Build the future with us

Are you passionate about artificial intelligence, automation, solving complex problems, and improving the way we work? Do you want to contribute to the purpose of a company that strives to ensure its clients feel confident and secure about their future? As an Intern – Artificial Intelligence, Automation and Operational Efficiency, you will play a key role in identifying, designing, and deploying innovative solutions aimed at optimizing our internal processes using artificial intelligence, Microsoft Copilot, the Power Platform, and other emerging technologies.

This position is a great opportunity to showcase your skills and fully realize your potential within a caring and trustworthy company. Here, people and their development are at the heart of our priorities, fostering an environment that encourages collaboration and innovation.

What You Will Accomplish With Us

As an Intern – Artificial Intelligence, Automation and Operational Efficiency, you will be at the core of our mission. Here are the main responsibilities:



- Design, develop and deploy automation and artificial intelligence solutions using Microsoft Copilot, Power Automate, Power Apps and other emerging technologies;
- Develop dashboards and visualizations in Power BI to make gains, performance indicators and improvement opportunities visible;
- Participate in the integration of solutions within the Microsoft 365 ecosystem and collaborate with internal teams to understand needs and propose innovative solutions;
- Develop proofs of concept (POCs), prototypes or intelligent agents to validate new automation and artificial intelligence approaches;
- Use artificial intelligence to reduce low-value-added tasks, accelerate decision-making and improve the employee experience;
- Participate in process optimization workshops to identify transformation and innovation opportunities;
- Document processes, developed solutions and realized benefits to facilitate their reuse and deployment.

What Could Accelerate Your Success In This Role

We are looking for someone who:



- Is currently pursuing a master’s degree in artificial intelligence, computer science, software engineering, analytics, information systems or a related field;
- Must complete a university-credited internship during the Winter 2027 semester;
- Stands out for their autonomy;
- Demonstrates great creativity;
- Shows resourcefulness and an ability to learn quickly in loosely defined environments;
- Is recognized for their analytical mindset;
- Demonstrates a strong interest in the practical use of artificial intelligence to solve business problems;
- Has a good knowledge of Microsoft 365, generative artificial intelligence tools and automation platforms;
- Enjoys exploring new ideas, experimenting and challenging traditional ways of doing things;
- Possesses excellent communication and collaboration skills with both technical and non-technical stakeholders;
- Must have an advanced level of French proficiency;
- Would be considered an asset if they have experience with Copilot Studio, Power Platform, Python, AI agents, process automation or technology prototype development.

Why you will love working with us



- A work environment where learning and development merge with a collective pursuit of excellence. 
- Artificial intelligence is in everyone's hands, enabling you to increase your personal efficiency and supporting the organization's growth. 
- A healthy, safe, fair, and inclusive environment where potential can be freely expressed and developed. 
- The possibility to work in a hybrid environment supported by flexibility and access to inspiring, innovative workspaces. 
- Student benefits: Access to internal training, mentoring, involvement in real projects, flexible schedules adapted to studies, and a rewarding experience for your professional journey.

Apply now and get ahead of your career, where your talent really belongs! Still unsure about applying?

At iA, we believe in potential and value diverse experiences. If this role inspires you, go ahead and apply – your place might be with us, and we want to get to know you!

The typical hiring range for this position is $27,50 to $30,50 CAD per hour; the base salary offered varies according to years of study and the position status (student or intern). At iA, we are committed to offering a fair, equitable, and market-based compensation structure. Our market data is updated annually to reflect the most current market conditions.
